The files in this directory come from lzma1 by Filip Seman, https://github.com/xseman/lzma1, under the Apache
License 2.0 in LICENSE here. They come from the fork on branch feat/lzma2-decoder at commit
19f319c68ed898619393a579d126ce06e3d5d704, which is lzma1 0.4.0 plus raw LZMA1 and LZMA2 decoding. lzma1 ports them
from XZ for Java (0BSD) by Lasse Collin and Igor Pavlov.

Copied: crc32.ts, hash234.ts, hc4.ts, header.ts, lz-decoder.ts, lz-encoder.ts, lzma-coder.ts, lzma-decoder.ts,
lzma-encoder.ts, lzma-encoder-fast.ts, lzma2-decoder.ts, range-coder.ts, range-decoder.ts and range-encoder.ts.

lzma-defuse changed them as follows, and the files then moved into archive-defuse unchanged.

In every file:
- Biome reformatted it to this package's style, with spaces for tabs and single quotes for double.
- Imports drop the ".js" suffix, since this package compiles to CommonJS.
- A first line names lzma1, its license and this NOTICE.

In lzma-decoder.ts and lzma-encoder.ts, the box-drawing characters around section comments are now "--", since this
package keeps its files ASCII.

In hc4.ts, lz-decoder.ts, lz-encoder.ts, lzma-encoder.ts, lzma2-decoder.ts and range-encoder.ts, each function that
assigned to its own parameter now copies the parameter into a local variable first. This package's lint rules forbid
the assignment. The arithmetic is the same.

In lzma-encoder-fast.ts:
- getNextSymbol() throws if no matches were read, where it used a non-null assertion.
- A chained assignment is now two assignments.

In lzma-encoder.ts, the empty body of the loop in encode() holds a comment.

In lzma2-decoder.ts:
- The file defines INPUT_MARGIN itself instead of importing it from alone-decoder.ts, which this package does not
  copy. The value is still 64.
- A private method, currentLzma(), returns the LZMA decoder or throws "LZMA2 chunk without properties". It replaces
  two non-null assertions.

crc32.ts, hash234.ts, header.ts, lzma-coder.ts, lzma-decoder.ts, range-coder.ts and range-decoder.ts have no changes
beyond formatting and imports.
